# ADHD Progress Hub

When this workspace (or the user) involves starting, resuming, migrating, or leaving half-finished work:

1. Call MCP `adhd-hub` → `resolve_project` with the workspace path (create if missing), then `session_digest` with the same path and a short query about the task.
2. Call `check_overlap` with the project/migration name before diving in. If hits look related, tell the user what was left open and offer to resume from the hub progress notes.
3. When work is left incomplete (migration paused, setup partial, plan not executed), call `upsert_progress` with `workspace_path` and/or `project_slug`, a concrete Done/Next/Blockers note, and `source_tool: "cursor"`. Also `upsert_thread` if this is a new unfinished thread.
4. When the user finishes, call `mark_done` on the thread id.
5. If the user asks to be reminded later, call `set_reminder`.

Do not invent hub state — only report what the tools return. Prefer summaries; never dump full chat transcripts into the hub.
